    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0347" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg313"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Julian</hi>: I take pleasure in repeating
                    the assurance which I gave you verbally yesterday when you handed me your note
                    of that date, that my Government will very heartily welcome the visit to
                    Washington of Sir Wilfrid Laurier, the prime minister of Canada, and Sir Louis
                    Davies, minister of marine, and that it cheerfully yields to the desire of the
                    Marquis of Salisbury to so far modify the character of the meeting of experts,
                    as set forth in Mr. Adam’s note of the 15th ultimo, as to admit the officials
                    named as well as yourself to the meeting, in order to watch the discussion and
                    suggest questions.</p>
                <p>I beg to add that Mr. John W. Foster, whom, as you know, the President has
                    intrusted with the negotiations relative to the seal question, will be expected
                    also to attend the meetings on the part of the United States.</p>
                <p>I take it for granted that the foregoing modification of the character of the
                    meeting does not in any wise relieve the experts from the duty of reaching
                    conclusions on their own behalf respecting the conditions of the Pribilof seal
                    herd and making a report thereon. I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
